  "id": "global-cumulative-hazard-indexes-chis",
  "stac_version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "This dataset provides monthly information on Cumulative Hazard Indices (CHIs) at global scale. CHI1, CHI3 and CHI4 describe surface conditions, while CHI2 includes two pressure levels, 2.5 and 200 dbar.\nEach dataset contains the estimated CHI and the related stressors used in its computation, with latitude, longitude and time dimensions, plus a level dimension for CHI2. The reference period used as a baseline for defining the climatology varies according to the input dataset required to build each CHI.\n\nCHI1 is provided globally at 1° × 1° spatial resolution, covering the period from 1993 to 2022.\nThe monthly-averaged input variables used to compute the stressors in CHI1 are sea surface temperature (SST) and hydrogen ion concentration (H+). CHI1 combines stressors associated with marine heatwaves, cold spells and ocean acidification.\n\nCHI2 is provided at global scale at 1° × 1° spatial resolution, covering January 2004 to November 2022.\nThe monthly-averaged input variables used to compute the stressors in CHI2 are temperature, dissolved oxygen (O2) and salinity, obtained from combined observational and model products. CHI2 combines stressors associated with marine heatwaves, cold spells, deoxygenation, low salinity and high salinity. CHI2 and its associated stressors are provided at two pressure levels: 2.5 dbar (level 0) and 200 dbar (level 1).\n\nCHI3 is provided globally at 1° × 1° spatial resolution, covering the period from 1993 to 2022.\nThe monthly-averaged input variables used to compute the stressors in CHI3 are SST, sea surface salinity (SSS), sea surface density (SSD), H+ and wind speed. CHI3 combines nine stressors associated with marine heatwaves, cold spells, ocean acidification, low and high SSS, low and high SSD, and low and high wind speed. Both low-wind events (< 10th percentile) and high-wind events (> 90th percentile) contribute to the same CHI3 index.\n\nCHI4 is provided at global scale at 1° × 1° spatial resolution, covering the period from 2012 to 2020.\nThe monthly-averaged input variables used to compute the stressors in CHI4 are SST and fishing effort (FE, expressed as hours spent fishing). CHI4 combines stressors associated with marine heatwaves, cold spells and high FE.",
